# Splitting "Table 2-C" into its two printed fragments changed two URLs that were
# already published. The UDC prints the citation twice -- residential districts on
# p56 and commercial on p70 -- and the single /table-2-c page only ever served the
# residential half, so that is where the old URL points. The commercial fragment
# had no URL at all before.
#
# These are citable legal-reference URLs; a 404 on one is worse than a redirect
# that lands a reader one click from where they meant to be.
/code/duluth/table-2-c    /code/duluth/table-2-c-residential    301
/code/duluth/table-2-c.md /code/duluth/table-2-c-residential.md 301
/code/duluth/table-2-d    /code/duluth/table-2-d-residential    301
/code/duluth/table-2-d.md /code/duluth/table-2-d-residential.md 301
